---
name: Fleet hardening
description: Default-deny egress, enforced pod security, a custom seccomp profile and runtime detection, rolled out one cluster at a time across Appwrite Cloud.
---

Appwrite Cloud runs customer code. In 2026 I led the work to make every production cluster assume that code is hostile.

Every pod now starts with no egress, and each service declares what it needs to reach. Kyverno enforces pod security on the cloud and edge clusters and audits the rest, and exceptions live in the repo of the service that needs them. Containers run under Appwrite's own seccomp profile. Tetragon watches for container-escape techniques and pages on-call when it sees one.

The hard part was the rollout. Each control went to staging first, then into audit mode on one production region, then into enforce mode one cluster at a time. Each step had an alert on dropped traffic, so a missing exception showed up in Grafana before a customer saw it.
